{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/656057-relic-design-question","id":656057,"title":"Relic design question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-07T22:14:59-07:00","id":656057,"title":"Relic design question","content":"So I am trying to design a relic for a scion of The Morrigan that is to be gifted upon reaching godhood. The scion's main purview is war and fertility. Followed by death and health. He is going for a druid feel. And trying to represent the cycle of death and renewal. The dead, blood, ashes and destruction of war lead to new growth for plants. Which in turn feed animal life. Including humans. That sort of thing. Anyway I was wanting to throw an idea out there. It was a spear that the haft was a still living branch with ivy on it. As it moves closer to the head of the spear it looks more burnt and dead. Then the spearhead rises out of the tip with a fuller on either side. From the shaft a liquid runs down the fuller at all times. It is a mix of blood and sap. Anything it lands on sprouts plant life native to the region. And when wounding a target it cause plants to grow out the wound. Even if the area is barren or normally unable to grow things it will cause nature to retake the land. Such as a parking lot. How does that sound? And I have no idea how it would work mechanically. I need some pointers. And help with a name. Please and thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7272-ratet","name":"Ratet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T18:53:39-07:00","id":661361,"title":"","content":"It sounds like a combination of Fertility disciplines here. The Level 1 Green thumb to let the plants grow for a hear without nutrients or care and the Level 6 Accelerate Growth. The tricky part is the Health component. I suppose you could accelerate the growth of the seeds many people ingest and having things grow right in their stomachs/digestive tracts. You are still looking at a 6 or 7 point relic here though to create those abilities from scratch.<br /> <br /> If the character in question already had these two boons (since you said it was for reaching godhood) then for say a 4 point Relic I could see an effect of 'Seed and area/wound and apply Green Thumb effects' on a Hasta templated item. Then they use their own Accelerate growth to make the effect instantaneous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T17:48:40-07:00","id":666235,"title":"","content":"I can't help with the mechanics, but for a name I can offer a few suggestions. You could go the easy route and simply name it Spear of {Character}, or some variation thereof. If you want a specific name for it like Mjolnir or Gungnir, then I would suggest an Irish Gaelic translation of something like Renewal or Rebirth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7395-meribson","name":"Meribson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7395_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T18:11:44-07:00","id":673690,"title":"","content":"That is a very good idea for the name. I have been struggling with that. Mostly since I suck at names. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7272-ratet","name":"Ratet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T18:14:10-07:00","id":673692,"title":"","content":"Hmmm. I guess that could work for how it goes. I didn't think to tie in boons for after. I was just trying for all at once sort of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7272-ratet","name":"Ratet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T10:07:14-07:00","id":676527,"title":"","content":"Bri Bolga. &quot;Spear of Life&quot; in bastardized Gaelic. Bri has a / diacritical on the I, but I'm not going to search for it here. Or Bri-a-fuil Bolga. &quot;Life's Blood Spear&quot;. Something like that. You can go get the declensions and mutations right if you want to poke around, but it is just a game, so it should probably do fine. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T12:14:15-07:00","id":679243,"title":"","content":"Those are awesome. I really like the second one the most.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7272-ratet","name":"Ratet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}